🚀 How to Run the Project

Step 1: Set Up the Database

Open MySQL and run:

create_database.sql
create_tables.sql
insert_data.sql

Step 2: Analyze the Data

Run:

analysis_queries.sql

to perform SQL-based analysis.

Step 3: Connect Power BI to MySQL
Open Microsoft Power BI Desktop.
Select Get Data.
Choose MySQL Database.
Enter the database server details.
Select the required tables.
Load the data into Power BI.
Step 4: Create Relationships

Create relationships between:

Properties and Schools
Properties and Sales
Customers and Sales
Agents and Sales
Step 5: Open the Dashboard

Open:

Real_Estate_Pricing_Dashboard.pbix

and explore the interactive dashboard.

